        "sha256": "040a60569e823a9a25eaae17e49e3755cb7aa1c60be6a61de82242af1283ccef"
      },
      "beforeText": "在线框以恒定角速度旋转、上述夹角均匀增大的模型中，选取计时起点，使此时法线与磁场同向，初始夹角为零。\n于是角 $\\alpha$ 随时间 t 按下式增大，其中角频率以 $\\omega$ 表示：\n$\\alpha=\\omega t$\n这里旋转角速度的大小就是磁通量振荡的角频率，单位为弧度每秒；通常的频率 f 表示每秒完成多少个周期，角频率等于频率乘以两倍圆周率。",
      "afterText": "采用最简单的匀速转动模型：线框的法线在一个包含磁场方向的平面内转动，计时起点选在线框法线与磁场同向的位置。\n下面等式中的角 $\\alpha$ 表示从这个起点连续累计的转角，也就是旋转相位；它不是始终取零到半周范围内的通常几何夹角。\n这一连续转角的余弦与线框法线和 B 的几何夹角的余弦相同，因此可以在前述磁通量公式中使用这一转角约定。\n在此约定下，转角随时间 t 均匀增大，其中角频率以 $\\omega$ 表示：\n$\\alpha=\\omega t$\n这里旋转角速度的大小就是磁通量振荡的角频率，单位为弧度每秒；通常的频率 f 表示每秒完成多少个周期，角频率等于频率乘以两倍圆周率。",
      "allOtherFieldsAndBlocksUnchanged": true
    },
    {
      "edition": "modern-us-neutral-en",
      "pointer": "/prose/9/text",
      "before": {
        "path": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/stemrobin-181-six/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d1816-d183-n21-text-author/frozen/modern-us-neutral-en/lesson.template.json",
        "bytes": 31717,
        "sha256": "a376f72b095f43c128d032c1715f15f2ac99342e368297cef451895dd4ae7e64"
      },
      "current": {
        "path": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/stemrobin-181-six/lemmadeck/.tmp/STEMROBIN-181/d1816-d194/work/adapt/10p/modern-us-neutral-en/lessons/phy10-c1-s3-n21/lesson.template.json",
        "bytes": 32148,
        "sha256": "037190ea8cc9402af0588beeb541d2068df05709977b15f476be1ebadcffad54"
      },
      "beforeText": "In the model where the loop rotates at constant angular speed and the specified angle increases uniformly, choose the time origin so that the normal initially points along the magnetic field and the initial angle is zero.\nThe angle $\\alpha$ then increases with time t as follows, with the angular frequency denoted by $\\omega$:\n$\\alpha=\\omega t$\nHere the magnitude of the rotational angular velocity is the angular frequency of the flux oscillation, measured in radians per second; ordinary frequency f counts cycles per second, and angular frequency is frequency multiplied by twice pi.",
      "afterText": "Use the simple uniform-rotation model in which the loop normal sweeps a plane containing the magnetic-field direction, and choose the time origin at the position where the normal points along the field.\nIn the equation below, the angle $\\alpha$ is the rotation angle accumulated continuously from that initial position, or rotational phase; it is not the principal geometric angle, which remains between zero and half a turn.\nThe cosine of this continuously accumulated rotation angle equals the cosine of the geometric angle between the loop normal and B, so this rotation-phase convention can be used in the preceding flux formula.\nUnder this convention, the rotation angle increases uniformly with time t, with the angular frequency denoted by $\\omega$:\n$\\alpha=\\omega t$\nHere the magnitude of the rotational angular velocity is the angular frequency of the flux oscillation, measured in radians per second; ordinary frequency f counts cycles per second, and angular frequency is frequency multiplied by twice pi.",
      "allOtherFieldsAndBlocksUnchanged": true
    }
  ],
